From: zyi
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: zero3w: enable the SoC RTC

The vendor board file disables the SoC RTC ("Disable soc rtc") in favour
of an external hym8563 that is not fitted on this board, so there was no
RTC at all: every boot started at the 2022 build date until NTP synced,
and nothing could arm an RTC wake-up. The board has the 32.768 kHz crystal
and VCC-RTC from the PMIC (schematic p.1), so enable rtc@7090000
(rtc-sunxi, CONFIG_AW_RTC=y). It becomes rtc0; the kernel config's
RTC_HCTOSYS/SYSTOHC device moves from rtc1 to rtc0 with it.

---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-orangepi-zero3w.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-orangepi-zero3w.dts
index 4622aed67..8eac000fd 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-orangepi-zero3w.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-orangepi-zero3w.dts
@@ -2544,9 +2544,15 @@ virtual-dc1sw2 {
 	};
 };
 
-/*Disable soc rtc*/
+/*
+ * SoC RTC on: the vendor template disabled it in favour of an external
+ * hym8563, which this board does not have (no /dev/rtc at all, the clock
+ * restarted in 2022 on every boot). The board has the 32.768 kHz crystal
+ * and VCC-RTC from the PMIC (schematic p.1), so the SoC RTC keeps time
+ * across reboots and while powered off with the supply connected.
+ */
 &rtc {
-	status = "disabled";
+	status = "okay";
 };
 
 &s_twi1 {
